  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing the Economic and Political Empowerment of Women in the Sava</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There is severe under-representation of women at all levels of government and decision-making in the three provinces which form the deprived Northern Region of Ghana. This is a significant factor preventing the economic, cultural and political advancement of women in the region. For instance, only 11% of women have any formal education. This project will provide training and support to women so they have the skills, confidence and abilities to stand for public office in local, district and parliamentary elections. There will also be a mentoring programme for those who secure public office, so that newly-elected officials can receive advice and guidance from more experienced peers. Women will also be linked up into networks and coalitions so that they can be effectively organised and get their voices heard on issues of policy. The project will actively involve community leaders including traditional chiefs as well as all the political parties (on a non-partisan basis), to garner their support for this initiative. As a result, and fitting in with the Millennium Development Goals (MDG), women&apos;s representation at all levels will increase and women&apos;s interests and rights, including to natural resources, services (including education), and participation in decision-making will have increased.</narrative>
  </description>
